## Static red basis (why the new test fails before the change)

1. `packages/extension-laya/tests/typed-decision.test.ts` imports
   `../src/typed-decision.ts`, which does not exist yet: every case fails at module
   load with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
2. Even with that module present, the manifest currently declares exactly three
   tools (`decision_choose`, `decision_test`, `decision_score`) and three
   implementations (`packages/extension-laya/tool-mode.extension.json:27-78`), so
   the DEC-06 manifest test fails on the expected five-tool/five-implementation
   lists, on the missing typed contract ids, and on the missing typed schema files.
3. The four typed schema files (`decision-test-typed.{input,output}.json`,
   `decision-score-typed.{input,output}.json`) do not exist, so the schema-exactness
   test fails on ENOENT.
4. `src/index.ts` handles only the three compatibility implementation ids
   (`laya-onnx-decision-*`), so typed invocations would throw
   `this extension implements the decision family, not "…-typed"` once wired.

## Green requires

- `src/typed-decision.ts` pure adapter/validation module;
- the four closed schema files and the two manifest tools/implementations;
- the typed branches in `src/index.ts` reusing `assertDecisionInputSafe` and
  `validateProbabilityDistribution`;
- the existing manifest assertion in `tests/laya-decision.test.ts` updated to five
  tools/five implementations (the compatibility trio is otherwise untouched);
- `npx tsx --test packages/extension-laya/tests/*.test.ts` and
  `npx tsc --noEmit -p packages/extension-laya/tsconfig.json` run green.
